SGLang patch on top of the vendored llama.cpp tree (ggml/, see ggml/LLAMA_CPP_COMMIT), applied after
0001-mmq-dst-type.patch.

MMQ: IQ1_M. llama.cpp's MMQ has no IQ1_M (it takes the MMVQ or the dequantize + cuBLAS path), and IQ1_M holds
most of the expert bytes in the ~1.75 bpw packs of the large MoE models. This adds a tile loader on the
Q8_0_16 tile layout (IQ2_XS's: int8 values and one float scale a 16-value group). An IQ1_M value is

  d * (2*s + 1) * ((g - 1) + delta)   g in {0, 1, 2} from iq1s_grid_gpu, delta = +-1/8 (IQ1M_DELTA)

with d the block's fp16 scale (the top nibbles of the four scale words), s the 3-bit scale of a 16-value
group and delta's sign from the qh bit of its 8-value group. It is stored as the int8 8*(g - 1) + (delta < 0 ?
-1 : 1) with the group's float scale d * (2*s + 1) / 8, so every value the int8 MMA multiplies is exact. The
config tables get IQ1_M entries next to IQ2_XS's (same layout and tile sizes), and a template instance.
tests/test_gguf.py checks the result against gguf-py's dequantization.

